/**
 * Opportunity records: the surfacing layer.
 *
 * WHAT THIS FILE IS. Each record is one place where a clinical decision cannot be made today and a
 * radiopharmaceutical might settle it. Records are written to be argued with: the unmet need, the
 * hypothesis, the study that would test it, the state of the public evidence in five due-diligence
 * domains, a red/amber/green flag on six review categories, and everyone else publicly working on it.
 *
 * HOW THEY WERE FOUND. Seven lenses, carried on the `lens` field:
 *   theranostic-gap       a therapy is in the clinic with no diagnostic paired to it
 *   standalone-diagnostic a companion diagnostic inside someone's therapy programme that would stand alone
 *   target-crossover      a target validated by an antibody, ADC or bispecific with no radioligand against it
 *   unmet-need-first      starts from a decision nobody can make, then asks which target could settle it
 *   non-us-registry       the work is registered outside ClinicalTrials.gov and invisible to pipeline tracking
 *   maturing-preclinical  preclinical evidence close enough to the clinic to belong in a clinical-stage funnel
 *   supply-isotope        the opportunity is production, supply, dosimetry or delivery, not the molecule
 *
 * WHY THERE IS NO SCORE. Evidence carries a state (strong/moderate/thin/none) with the fact and the
 * source behind it, and each review category carries a flag with its reason. A single total out of
 * five hides the reason and stops discriminating between candidates once you have more than a handful.
 *
 * SOURCING. Every figure in this file was read from a public primary source in the session that wrote
 * it, and the URL is on the record. Where a number exists only in a conference abstract, investor
 * material or a secondary review, the record says so. Where something does not exist, the record says
 * that too: opp-her3-imaging-crossover and opp-alpha-synuclein-pet-parkinsons are deliberate worked
 * negatives, kept because the reasoning is the useful part.
 *
 * SCOPE. Everything in the public domain is in scope: any target, indication, isotope, company or
 * geography. The one thing never recorded is non-public information. The computed layer at
 * /universe/ideas/ extends these hand-written records to every cross-link in the public data.
 */
