    differentiation: "The comparators are CT, which leaves a 41.4% futile-laparotomy rate, and staging laparoscopy, which is itself an operation. CA 19-9 is neither sensitive nor specific enough to decide resectability, and FDG PET is not standard in this disease. FAP imaging is differentiated because pancreatic cancer is the tumour where the stromal target is most abundant and FDG performs worst.",
